abstract: |-
  abstract: |
    This repository contains the complete source code and simulation framework 
    developed for the master's thesis evaluating the performance of Wi-Fi 7 
    (IEEE 802.11be) networks. The simulations are implemented using the ns-3 
    network simulator and include various scenarios to assess key performance 
    metrics including throughput, Packet Delivery Ratio (PDR), end-to-end delay, 
    and jitter. The framework supports multiple experimental configurations 
    with varying node density (10-100 nodes), mobility speed (5-25 m/s), 
    traffic load (100-1000 Kbps), and SNR levels (5-30 dB). Additionally, 
    the code includes Multi-Link Operation (MLO) capability testing and 
    energy consumption analysis. Automated bash scripts enable batch execution 
    of experiments across different parameter sweeps, while Python scripts 
    provide data processing, statistical analysis, and visualization of results. 
    This code is intended to support reproducibility and further research 
    in next-generation wireless networks.
